    "description": "If you like Naked's grass-fed sourcing but need a sport certification, Transparent Labs is the alternative. Its whey isolate, which comes in an unflavored version among many flavors, gives 28 g of protein in a scoop of about 32 g, per the brand at the time of writing. It is Informed Choice and Informed Protein certified. At list price it costs a little less per gram than Naked Whey Isolate, and a serving is one scoop rather than two.",
    "pros": [
      "Informed Choice and Informed Protein certified, per the brand",
      "Unflavored version available alongside many flavors",
      "28 g of protein per single scoop"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "More expensive per gram than standard Naked Whey",
      "Flavored versions add sweeteners and flavors"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick for tested athletes who want a grass-fed, unflavored isolate.",
